<Legal
  title="Terms of use"
  intro="The agreement between you and MYAH when you use myahsits.com, as a house and pet sitter or as a home owner."
  updated="2 October 2026"
>
  <div class="lg-card"><p>In short: MYAH helps sitters and owners find each other and arrange sits. The sit itself is an agreement between the sitter and the owner. Be honest, be kind, and look after each other's homes and animals.</p></div>

  <h2>1. About MYAH</h2>
  <p>MYAH (myahsits.com) is run by its founders, Callum &amp; Niamh. You can contact us at <a href="mailto:hello@myahsits.com">hello@myahsits.com</a>. By creating an account or using the site you agree to these terms and to our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>2. Your account</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You must be 18 or over.</li>
    <li>Sign up as a sitter or as a home owner, and keep your details accurate and up to date.</li>
    <li>Keep your password private. You are responsible for what happens on your account.</li>
    <li>One person (or one couple, for a joint sitter account) per account.</li>
    <li>Complete ID verification, with your own genuine documents, before applying, posting, messaging or confirming a sit.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. What MYAH does, and doesn't do</h2>
  <p>MYAH gives sitters a public page, lets owners post sits, and lets members apply, message and confirm sits with each other. We are not a party to the arrangement between a sitter and an owner, and we do not employ sitters.</p>
  <p>Everyone on MYAH is ID checked: before you can apply for sits, post a sit, message other members or confirm a sitter, you send a photo of your passport or driving licence and a selfie, and we check that they match. A verified badge means that check was completed; it is not a background or criminal record check. Owners and sitters should still talk, check reviews and references, and agree the details of every sit between themselves.</p>

  <h2>4. Membership is free</h2>
  <p>MYAH is completely free to use: creating a profile, posting sits, applying, messaging and confirming sitters all cost nothing. If we ever introduce paid features, we will tell you well in advance, and nothing will ever be charged without your clear agreement.</p>

  <h2>5. Sitters</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Describe your experience truthfully, and only post reviews that are real.</li>
    <li>Only apply for sits you can do, and tell the owner straight away if your plans change.</li>
    <li>During a sit, follow the owner's care routines, look after the home as your own, and contact a vet or the emergency services first if an animal or person is in danger.</li>
    <li>Keep the owner's private details (address, codes, wifi and contacts) to yourself, and use them only for the sit.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Home owners</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Describe your home, pets and their needs accurately, including any medical or behavioural needs.</li>
    <li>Make sure your home is safe for a sitter, and that you are allowed to have a sitter stay (for example under your tenancy or insurance).</li>
    <li>Leave clear instructions, vet details and an emergency contact.</li>
    <li>Arrange your own home and pet insurance. MYAH does not insure homes, pets or sitters.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Your content</h2>
  <p>You keep ownership of the photos, words and reviews you add. You give MYAH permission to show them on the site so the service works, for as long as they are on your account. Only upload content you have the right to share, and nothing unlawful, misleading or offensive.</p>

  <h2>8. Messages and behaviour</h2>
  <p>Be respectful. Do not harass anyone, share anyone else's personal details without permission, or use MYAH to send spam or to arrange anything unlawful. You can report anything that worries you to <a href="mailto:hello@myahsits.com">hello@myahsits.com</a>.</p>

  <h2>9. Suspending or closing accounts</h2>
  <p>You can ask us to close your account at any time. We may suspend or close an account that breaks these terms, puts other members, homes or animals at risk, or is used fraudulently. Where it is safe to, we will tell you why.</p>

  <h2>10. Our responsibility to you</h2>
  <p>We work to keep MYAH running smoothly and securely, but we cannot promise it will always be available or free of errors. Because the sit is arranged between members, we are not responsible for what happens during a sit, or for loss or damage caused by a member. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law, such as for death or personal injury caused by negligence, or your rights as a consumer.</p>

  <h2>11. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>We may update these terms as MYAH grows. We will change the date at the top and, for significant changes, tell you by email or on the site before they apply.</p>

  <h2>12. Law</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales, and the courts of England and Wales have jurisdiction. If you live elsewhere in the UK, you can also bring proceedings in your local courts.</p>
</Legal>
